# orders its pre-settle RoCE barriers on the stream (roce.ordered_barriers): before each eager RoCE gather an NCCL
# all-gather on the same stream, no torch.cuda.synchronize. A GPU still starts the RoCE gather only after every rank's
# GPU reached the same gather's NCCL step (NCCL waits without a limit), so a rank still building or compiling holds
# the others in NCCL, never in the 20 s RoCE wait (the first-start guarantee RoceComm.settle names); what goes is the
# host's wait after every gather. Timed startup work (calibration, the prompt-layer timing, fcost) keeps the host
# barrier. TF_ROCE_ORDERED_BARRIERS=0: the host barrier as before (the old path; ranks may differ: both forms are
# the same one-float NCCL all-gather). Boot only; replies unchanged.
