+    guarantee ``RoceComm.settle`` describes holds as before: a GPU starts the RoCE gather only after that NCCL
+    all-gather completes (stream order), which needs every rank's GPU to have reached the same gather's NCCL step,
+    and NCCL waits without a limit; so a rank still building an extension or compiling a kernel holds the others in
+    NCCL, never in a RoCE wait (TF_ROCE_WAIT_S). What goes is the host's wait for the GPU after every gather (the
+    barrier's ``torch.cuda.synchronize``), which serialised an eager window's launches with its kernels.
